      {
        "id": "p58-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x}{x^2-9}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\ln|x^2-9|+C$",
          "worked": "The denominator is $f(x)=x^2-9$, so $f'(x)=2x$. No adjustment is needed.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int\\frac{2x}{x^2-9}\\,dx&=\\ln|x^2-9|+C\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{6x+1}{3x^2+x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\ln|3x^2+x|+C$",
          "worked": "The denominator is $f(x)=3x^2+x$, so $f'(x)=6x+1$. No adjustment is needed.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int\\frac{6x+1}{3x^2+x}\\,dx&=\\ln|3x^2+x|+C\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x+1}{x^2+x-3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\ln|x^2+x-3|+C$",
          "worked": "The denominator is $f(x)=x^2+x-3$, so $f'(x)=2x+1$. No adjustment is needed.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int\\frac{2x+1}{x^2+x-3}\\,dx&=\\ln|x^2+x-3|+C\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{5-6x}{2+5x-3x^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\ln|2+5x-3x^2|+C$",
          "worked": "The denominator is $f(x)=2+5x-3x^2$, so $f'(x)=5-6x$. No adjustment is needed.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int\\frac{5-6x}{2+5x-3x^2}\\,dx&=\\ln|2+5x-3x^2|+C\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q5-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x+3}{x^2+6x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac12\\ln|x^2+6x-1|+C$",
          "worked": "The denominator is $f(x)=x^2+6x-1$, so $f'(x)=2x+6=2(x+3)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int\\frac{x+3}{x^2+6x-1}\\,dx&=\\frac12\\int\\frac{2x+6}{x^2+6x-1}\\,dx\\\\&=\\frac12\\ln|x^2+6x-1|+C\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q5-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{3-x}{12x-3-2x^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac14\\ln|12x-3-2x^2|+C$",
          "worked": "The denominator is $f(x)=12x-3-2x^2$, so $f'(x)=12-4x=4(3-x)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int\\frac{3-x}{12x-3-2x^2}\\,dx&=\\frac14\\int\\frac{12-4x}{12x-3-2x^2}\\,dx\\\\&=\\frac14\\ln|12x-3-2x^2|+C\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q5-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{e^x}{1+e^x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\ln(1+e^x)+C$",
          "worked": "The denominator is $f(x)=1+e^x$, so $f'(x)=e^x$. No adjustment is needed.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int\\frac{e^x}{1+e^x}\\,dx&=\\ln(1+e^x)+C\\end{align*}$$\nAbsolute value signs are unnecessary because $1+e^x>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q5-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{e^{-x}}{1+e^{-x}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\ln(1+e^{-x})+C$",
          "worked": "The denominator is $f(x)=1+e^{-x}$, so $f'(x)=-e^{-x}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int\\frac{e^{-x}}{1+e^{-x}}\\,dx&=-\\int\\frac{-e^{-x}}{1+e^{-x}}\\,dx\\\\&=-\\ln(1+e^{-x})+C\\end{align*}$$\nAbsolute value signs are unnecessary because $1+e^{-x}>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q5-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{e^x-e^{-x}}{e^x+e^{-x}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\ln(e^x+e^{-x})+C$",
          "worked": "The denominator is $f(x)=e^x+e^{-x}$, so $f'(x)=e^x-e^{-x}$. No adjustment is needed.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}{e^x+e^{-x}}\\,dx&=\\ln(e^x+e^{-x})+C\\end{align*}$$\nAbsolute value signs are unnecessary because $e^x+e^{-x}>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
